<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farrārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to spelt</i>, and in gen.
				<i>to corn</i> or <i>grain.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fistula,</span>”
				<i>a sort of hand-mill for corn</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 10, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 10, 23, §
			97</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farrārĭa</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n., <i>a
				granary</i>, <i>hay-loft</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
